<title>FRANCE: Thomson says bought no CSF shrs.</title>
<headline>Thomson says bought no CSF shrs.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned company Thomson SA said in a statement that it denied a newspaper article, in France's L'Agefi, which said it had been buying shares in its defence electronics unit Thomson-CSF.</p>
<p>The company said that it owned 51.53 percent in Thomson-CSF directly and another 6.78 percent through Sofivision.</p>
<p>Because these shares have double voting rights Thomson SA has a 73.26 stake in the voting stock of Thomson-CSF.</p>
<p>The government plans to sell the stake in Thomson-CSF and Lagardere Groupe and Alcatel Alsthom with Dassault Industries are allowed to bid for the stake.</p>
<p>Alcatel's chairman, Serge Tchuruk, and Dassault's Serge Dassault will on Tuesday morning jointly host a press briefing on their plans with Thomson-CSF.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
